We are given the following system of equations in three variables $ x, y, z $: $$
\begin{cases}
x^2 y + y^2 z = 1040 \quad \text{(1)} \\
x^2 z + z^2 y = 260 \quad \text{(2)} \\
(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) = -540 \quad \text{(3)}
\end{cases}
$$

Factor out $ (y - z) $: $$
(x^2 + y z)(y - z) = 780 \quad \text{(4)}
$$

We are given: $$
(x - y)(y - z)(z - x) = -540 \quad \text{(3)}
$$
